# GSD Configuration

# GitHub Standard Development Configuration
# This file defines the standards and workflows for this project

## Code Quality Standards

### Linting
- ESLint with TypeScript support
- Maximum 50 warnings allowed
- Auto-fixable issues should be fixed automatically

### Formatting
- Prettier for consistent code formatting
- Applied to TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON, and Markdown files

### Type Checking
- Strict TypeScript configuration
- No implicit any types
- Full type coverage required

### Testing
- Minimum 80% code coverage
- Unit tests for all modules
- Integration tests for critical paths
- E2E tests for user workflows

## Git Workflow

### Branch Naming
- `feature/` - New features
- `bugfix/` - Bug fixes
- `hotfix/` - Critical fixes
- `refactor/` - Code refactoring

### Commit Messages
- Use conventional commits format
- `feat:` - New features
- `fix:` - Bug fixes
- `docs:` - Documentation
- `style:` - Code style changes
- `refactor:` - Code refactoring
- `test:` - Testing
- `chore:` - Maintenance

### Pull Requests
- Require review for main/develop branches
- Must pass all CI checks
- Include tests for new features
- Update documentation as needed

## Development Workflow

### Pre-commit Hooks
- Lint code
- Format code
- Run type checking
- Run unit tests

### Pre-push Hooks
- Full test suite (for protected branches)
- Coverage checks
- Security audit

### CI/CD Pipeline
- Code quality checks
- Security audit
- Build verification
- Test execution
- Coverage reporting

## Tooling

### Required Tools
- Node.js 18+
- pnpm
- Git
- Docker (for local development)

### Development Scripts
- `pnpm gsd:setup` - Initialize GSD workflow
- `pnpm gsd:check` - Run all quality checks
- `pnpm gsd:fix` - Auto-fix issues
- `pnpm lint` - Run linter
- `pnpm format` - Format code
- `pnpm typecheck` - Run type checker
- `pnpm test:ci` - Run tests for CI